<title>GREECE: BEFORE THE BELL: STOCKS TRADE EX-DIV, EX-BONUS MON.</title>
<headline>BEFORE THE BELL: STOCKS TRADE EX-DIV, EX-BONUS MON.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Athens stock exchange said</p>
<p>the following shares will trade ex-dividend on Monday:</p>
<p>COMPANY		  DIVIDEND/SHARE     ADJUSTED PRICE</p>
<p>Intertyp		  25		   1,095</p>
<p>Imperio		  100		   2,470</p>
<p>Olympic Technical     42		   1,108</p>
<p>Fintexport		40		     860</p>
<p>Delta		     70		   3,290</p>
<p>Ellatex		   55		     845</p>
<p>Etma			20		     370</p>
<p>Sigalas		   28		     502</p>
<p>Vernicos		 120		   2,630</p>
<p>Ergas		     80		   1,395</p>
<p>Gekat		    120		   1,630</p>
<p>Konstantinidis	  55		     900</p>
<p>Bitros		    40		     960</p>
<p>Viosol		     6.5 interest	129</p>
<p>Proodeftiki	     70		   1,461</p>
<p>Remek		     19		     589</p>
<p>Mohlos		    24		   1,476</p>
<p>European Reliance     53		   1,231</p>
<p>National Insurance    60		   4,582</p>
<p>Also on Monday, the following shares will trade ex-bonus:</p>
<p>COMPANY	    ADJUSTED PRICE	 TERMS</p>
<p>Ionian Bank	   5,069	     3 bonus per 10 held</p>
<p>Proodeftiki	   1,461	     3 bonus per 10 held</p>
<p>National Insurance  4,582	     1 bonus per 10 held</p>
<p>Remek		     589	     3 bonus per 10 held</p>
<p>European Reliance   1,231	     3 bonus per 10 held</p>
<p>--George Georgiopoulos, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
